<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ Sun Alliance plays catch-up, adds Royal prefix.</title>
<headline>NZ Sun Alliance plays catch-up, adds Royal prefix.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Zealand division of British insurer Royal &amp; Sun Alliance on Monday changed all its local operating units' names in line with company policy to Royal SunAlliance from Sun Alliance.</p>
<p>The division had been out of line with its parent company because Sun Alliance in New Zealand had merged with Royal Insurance locally, without changing its name, a few years before the British parents did in 1996.</p>
<p>--Wellington newsroom +64 4 471 4273</p>
</text>
